@startuml SSD-ProcessSale
' ===========================================================================
' POS System - System Sequence Diagram: Process Sale (main success scenario)
' Software Engineering Practice - Part 2, artifact 1 (third element)
'
' The :System under design: is a BLACK BOX - only events crossing the system
' boundary are shown, never internal objects.
' ===========================================================================
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #1F4E79
  ActorBorderColor #1F4E79
  ActorBackgroundColor #DEEAF6
  LifeLineBorderColor #1F4E79
  ParticipantBorderColor #1F4E79
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #DEEAF6
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #D6B656
}

actor "Cashier" as Cashier
participant ":System" as System

activate System

Cashier -> System : makeNewSale()
activate System
System --> Cashier : «create» a sale

Cashier -> System : enterItem(itemID, quantity)
System --> Cashier : description, total

Cashier -> System : enterItem(itemID, quantity)
System --> Cashier : description, total

Cashier -> System : removeItem(itemID)   ' optional, loop [more items]

Cashier -> System : getTotal()
System --> Cashier : total

Cashier -> System : makePayment(cashTendered)
System --> Cashier : change due

Cashier -> System : endSale()
System --> Cashier : receipt

deactivate System
deactivate System

note right of System
  **System events** (messages from an actor to the system):
  makeNewSale, enterItem, removeItem, getTotal,
  makePayment, endSale.

  Each becomes a **system operation** on the facade controller
  (Register) during object design - see the OO design diagrams.
end note

@enduml
